      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T11:43:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s unlikely we\u0027ll have a 3rd style, but I thought it would be easier to understand if we had named constants. Compare :\n\n    connect(true, true, true, true)\n    connect(true, true, true, WAIT_FOR_CALLBACK)\n\nI think the latter is more readable.\n\nI could make it a boolean and say that WAIT_FOR_CALLBACK\u003dtrue and WAIT_FOR_IDLE\u003dfalse, but considering booleans are 32bits too, I think the current code is more capable with no real drawback.\n\nIf you feel strongly about this I\u0027m happy to change it.",
